==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|dis}}

===Etymology===
Originated in {{w|Jamaican Vernacular English}} or {{w|African American Vernacular English}}, probably originally short for ''[[disrespect]]'' or ''[[disparage]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dɪs/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪs}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|diss|es}}

# {{US|British|slang}} To put (someone) down, or show [[disrespect]] by the use of [[insulting]] [[language]] or [[dismissive]] [[behaviour]].

